# Measured zenith sky brightness used to calibrate the skyglow model in gen_light_pollution.py.
#
# Source: C. C. M. Kyba et al., "Worldwide variations in artificial skyglow", Scientific Reports 5,
# 8409 (2015), doi:10.1038/srep08409, CC BY 4.0. Supplementary Tables S2 (latitude, longitude) and
# S3 ("Clear": median clear, moonless sky brightness near local midnight in 2011-2012, in
# mag_SQM/arcsec^2; values the paper marks with * are the 28th percentile at sites without cloud
# reports). Sites 1-45, in the paper's order; sites 46-52 are left out, as the paper does, because
# of instrument problems. Site 33 is the second SQM at site 32 and is kept: the fit weights Berlin
# Steglitz twice.
#
# Format: name|latitude (deg N)|longitude (deg E)|clear-sky brightness (mag/arcsec^2)
